From 5f0dade166c70df0a4c59deb28f689ed4a333250 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Schwinn Saereesitthipitak <schwinns@nvidia.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 16:44:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] [KV Connector] Add checkpoint_prepare and
 checkpoint_restore connector hooks

Let KV connectors release what a process checkpoint must not contain, such
as transports and peer state, and rebuild it on restore. The engine calls
the scheduler-side instance before the workers on prepare and after them on
restore. The defaults do nothing.

An engine with a KV connector prepares only if the connector supports
process checkpoints with its config. supports_checkpoint is False by
default, and a MultiConnector needs every child to support them.

Signed-off-by: Schwinn Saereesitthipitak <schwinns@nvidia.com>
(cherry picked from commit cdc403d59109fb897e4a184d463570bf998b2a2f)
